## Solution

```matlab
function [x_hat_new, P_new] = ekf_prediction_step(x_hat, u, P, Q, dt)
    % EKF Prediction Step
    % Inputs:
    %   x_hat: current state estimate [x; y; theta]
    %   u: control input [v; omega]
    %   P: current covariance matrix
    %   Q: process noise covariance
    %   dt: time step
    % Outputs:
    %   x_hat_new: predicted state
    %   P_new: predicted covariance

    % Extract states
    x = x_hat(1);
    y = x_hat(2);
    theta = x_hat(3);

    % Extract inputs
    v = u(1);
    omega = u(2);

    % Prediction: propagate state using nonlinear motion model
    x_new = x + v * cos(theta) * dt;
    y_new = y + v * sin(theta) * dt;
    theta_new = theta + omega * dt;

    x_hat_new = [x_new; y_new; theta_new];

    % Compute Jacobian F = ∂f/∂x
    F = [1, 0, -v * sin(theta) * dt;
         0, 1,  v * cos(theta) * dt;
         0, 0,  1];

    % Update covariance: P = F * P * F' + Q
    P_new = F * P * F' + Q;
end
```

The key insight is that the Jacobian captures how errors in the angle θ affect the propagation of x and y positions (via the ∂/∂θ terms), while the covariance update shows how uncertainty grows through the nonlinear motion model.

