## Solution

```vhdl
library IEEE;
use IEEE.STD_LOGIC_1164.ALL;

entity majority_detector is
  port (
    A : in STD_LOGIC;
    B : in STD_LOGIC;
    C : in STD_LOGIC;
    Y : out STD_LOGIC
  );
end majority_detector;

architecture combinational of majority_detector is
begin
  -- Output is 1 when at least 2 inputs are 1
  -- This occurs when: AB + AC + BC
  Y <= (A AND B) OR (A AND C) OR (B AND C);
end combinational;
```

**Explanation:**

The majority function is true when any two or more inputs are 1. The Boolean expression captures all combinations:
- AB covers cases where both A and B are 1
- AC covers cases where both A and C are 1
- BC covers cases where both B and C are 1

These three product terms are ORed together to produce the final output. This is a standard combinational logic design that will synthesize into a minimal gate configuration on an FPGA.

